as to why he was on hiatus, right?

00:24:13.681 --> 00:24:14.778
- Yeah, no one knew.

00:24:14.778 --> 00:24:16.736
- They normally don't
usually give reasons.

00:24:16.736 --> 00:24:18.194
They just like-

00:24:18.194 --> 00:24:20.268
- People are extremely versatile.

00:24:20.268 --> 00:24:23.998
- "He/she is on hiatus,
just deal with it."

00:24:23.998 --> 00:24:25.385
But, yeah, apparently, I guess.

00:24:25.385 --> 00:24:26.400
I don't know.

00:24:26.400 --> 00:24:29.062
Was he sick or was it
just completely sudden?

00:24:29.062 --> 00:24:30.312
- I don't know.

00:24:31.270 --> 00:24:32.385
At the time of recording,

00:24:32.385 --> 00:24:34.458
I haven't read enough about what happened

00:24:34.458 --> 00:24:36.930
to know if it was like a
reoccurring health problem

00:24:36.930 --> 00:24:39.596
or if it was just a sudden thing.

00:24:39.596 --> 00:24:41.274
But man, like we all know

00:24:41.274 --> 00:24:44.907
how much pressure manga
artists get put through anyway

00:24:44.907 --> 00:24:48.330
and how much work they have
to do on a weekly basis.

00:24:48.330 --> 00:24:49.553
I mean, it's crazy to think

00:24:49.553 --> 00:24:53.209
that most of the big manga
artists we know about,

00:24:53.209 --> 00:24:55.120
you know, working shonen jump or whatever,

00:24:55.120 --> 00:24:57.154
get like two weeks off.

00:24:57.154 --> 00:24:59.151
No, less than two weeks
off every year, right?

00:24:59.151 --> 00:25:01.697
- It's like golden week and
then like one extra week.

00:25:01.697 --> 00:25:03.883
- I doubt they take it as
well. I doubt they take it.

00:25:03.883 --> 00:25:05.825
- And they don't really, I
doubt they take it off as well.

00:25:05.825 --> 00:25:07.474
It's just one week where they are forced

00:25:07.474 --> 00:25:08.528
to take a break, right?

00:25:08.528 --> 00:25:10.998
- I mean, I wasn't too
familiar with "Berserk."

00:25:10.998 --> 00:25:13.641
I'd only watched the 90s anime.

00:25:13.641 --> 00:25:14.778
- That's familiar enough.

00:25:14.778 --> 00:25:15.921
- I really enjoyed.

00:25:15.921 --> 00:25:16.844
It was very good.

00:25:16.844 --> 00:25:18.302
- It's great.

00:25:18.302 --> 00:25:19.760
- Fuck, I mean,

00:25:19.760 --> 00:25:22.225
it's just kind of sad hearing
like a legend of the industry

00:25:22.225 --> 00:25:24.388
who's kind of influenced a
lot of things that we've done.

00:25:24.388 --> 00:25:25.346
- Yeah.

00:25:25.346 --> 00:25:27.884
'Cause I remember we were
filming another project

00:25:27.884 --> 00:25:29.615
when the news broke to us,

00:25:29.615 --> 00:25:31.436
and it didn't hit me immediately

00:25:31.436 --> 00:25:34.172
because I was in like work
mode, I was in filming mode,

00:25:34.172 --> 00:25:36.556
so I was like, "Okay, I
gotta do this, this, this."

00:25:36.556 --> 00:25:39.164
And then it got home,
listened to Guts' theme once,

00:25:39.164 --> 00:25:41.988
and it just played continuously
for like the entire night.

00:25:41.988 --> 00:25:44.953
And I'm just sitting
there just like fucking,

00:25:44.953 --> 00:25:47.228
like part of my soul had died.

00:25:47.228 --> 00:25:49.133
- Yeah, I literally went
home and I was like,

00:25:49.133 --> 00:25:50.575
"I'm gonna reread 'Berserk.'"

00:25:50.575 --> 00:25:52.383
- Yeah, I feel like everyone did.

00:25:52.383 --> 00:25:53.468
- I started reading it.

00:25:53.468 --> 00:25:57.012
- I couldn't get past volume
one without feeling like,

00:25:57.012 --> 00:25:59.224
this fucking wave of like, oh fuck.

00:25:59.224 --> 00:26:01.866
- Yeah, 'cause like I always know

00:26:01.866 --> 00:26:04.464
that "Berserk" is one
of the greatest manga

00:26:04.464 --> 00:26:05.719
that has ever been made.

00:26:05.719 --> 00:26:07.700
And then going back home and realizing,

00:26:07.700 --> 00:26:11.422
just remembering everything
that was in this story

00:26:11.422 --> 00:26:14.531
and in this manga, it just
hit even fucking harder

00:26:14.531 --> 00:26:17.847
because I just had
forgotten how good it was

00:26:17.847 --> 00:26:20.092
before I really took the time to remember

00:26:20.092 --> 00:26:23.583
what it had achieved and
some of its greatest moments.

00:26:23.583 --> 00:26:25.086
If you hadn't read "Berserk,"

00:26:25.086 --> 00:26:28.620
there's always a perfect
time to read "Berserk"

00:26:28.620 --> 00:26:31.334
because anytime is the perfect
time to read "Berserk."

00:26:31.334 --> 00:26:32.733
So, please read fucking "Berserk."

00:26:32.733 --> 00:26:33.629
It's amazing.

00:26:33.629 --> 00:26:35.426
- I mean the manga single-handedly

00:26:35.426 --> 00:26:37.525
inspired the Dark Souls series.

00:26:37.525 --> 00:26:38.859
- I mean, it inspired a lot.

00:26:38.859 --> 00:26:39.892
It wasn't just Dark Souls.

00:26:39.892 --> 00:26:41.546
A lot of things wouldn't exist right now

00:26:41.546 --> 00:26:42.455
if not for "Berserk."

00:26:42.455 --> 00:26:43.288
- [Joey] Oh yeah.

00:26:43.288 --> 00:26:45.309
- And I don't know what
it is about "Berserk,"

00:26:45.309 --> 00:26:46.297
but it's literally like,

00:26:46.297 --> 00:26:50.550
it's literally the one
show, or not even one show,

00:26:50.550 --> 00:26:52.620
the one story or the one manga

00:26:52.620 --> 00:26:55.780
that seems to be like no matter
how tough this person is,

00:26:55.780 --> 00:26:59.447
no matter how like detached
they are from the world

00:26:59.447 --> 00:27:02.556
or whatever, "Berserk"
seems to be that one story

00:27:02.556 --> 00:27:05.005
that seems to be able to
affect anyone who reads it.

00:27:05.005 --> 00:27:07.688
- Yeah, because like
fundamentally, you know,

00:27:07.688 --> 00:27:09.562
it's like this whole
like dark fantasy thing

00:27:09.562 --> 00:27:10.734
with these like mythical creatures

00:27:10.734 --> 00:27:13.625
and it's bloody, gory and, you know, epic.

00:27:13.625 --> 00:27:17.441
But like the main themes
mostly are just like,

00:27:17.441 --> 00:27:19.945
you know, one person trying to figure out

00:27:19.945 --> 00:27:21.413
what the fuck they want to do in life.

00:27:21.413 --> 00:27:22.674
And like that's a theme

00:27:22.674 --> 00:27:24.854
that literally anyone
can get behind, right?

00:27:24.854 --> 00:27:29.614
Like, I'm kind of in this world,
shit's happening around me,

00:27:29.614 --> 00:27:32.337
I don't really know what
my purpose is in life.

00:27:32.337 --> 00:27:33.420
- I forgot how brutal it was.

00:27:33.420 --> 00:27:34.753
- It's brutal.

00:27:34.753 --> 00:27:36.788
- Again, I watched all the 90s anime.

00:27:36.788 --> 00:27:38.128
And I was like, holy shit.

00:27:38.128 --> 00:27:39.901
- The 90s anime is brutal as fuck.

00:27:39.901 --> 00:27:41.102
- I was like, "What the fuck?"

00:27:41.102 --> 00:27:42.300
I was like, "Oh my God."

00:27:42.300 --> 00:27:43.997
Like, it's just like, fuck.

00:27:43.997 --> 00:27:45.830
It just hurts to read.

00:27:46.782 --> 00:27:47.615
- [Garnt] It does.

00:27:47.615 --> 00:27:48.761
- It's so uncomfortable at times.

00:27:48.761 --> 00:27:50.571
- Yeah, and I think it's incredible

00:27:50.571 --> 00:27:53.453
because it is really,
really fucking brutal.

00:27:53.453 --> 00:27:54.313
There are some like,

00:27:54.313 --> 00:27:57.552
like his art, obviously we
haven't talked about his art yet.

00:27:57.552 --> 00:27:59.458
It's like some of the
best art to ever exist

00:27:59.458 --> 00:28:01.369
in the world of manga.

00:28:01.369 --> 00:28:05.523
Like, some of the horrific
imagery he managed to conjure up

00:28:05.523 --> 00:28:08.012
and some of like the creature designs

00:28:08.012 --> 00:28:09.703
and everything were
just something straight

00:28:09.703 --> 00:28:10.895
out of a nightmare, you know?

00:28:10.895 --> 00:28:14.403
And it's a brutal show and
it's an action packed show

00:28:14.403 --> 00:28:15.236
as well.

00:28:15.236 --> 00:28:19.013
Guts is like one of the biggest
badasses in anime and manga.

00:28:19.013 --> 00:28:21.430
And yet having said all that,

00:28:22.301 --> 00:28:24.687
the moments that people remember are

00:28:24.687 --> 00:28:26.718
like the really intimate moments,

00:28:26.718 --> 00:28:28.397
which isn't what you think

00:28:28.397 --> 00:28:30.294
if you looked at "Berserk"
on a surface level, right?

00:28:30.294 --> 00:28:32.475
You look at "Berserk" you
see these horrific creatures,

00:28:32.475 --> 00:28:35.118
you see Guts with a massive
sword tearing shit up,

00:28:35.118 --> 00:28:36.897
and you're like, "Yeah!

00:28:36.897 --> 00:28:38.547
"This is a manly man show."

00:28:38.547 --> 00:28:41.545
And you read it and you're
just like fucking crying inside

00:28:41.545 --> 00:28:43.640
because, you know, you see,

00:28:43.640 --> 00:28:46.549
trying to see Guts like
get through his trauma

00:28:46.549 --> 00:28:48.474
and find his journey and
everything like that.

00:28:48.474 --> 00:28:50.145
It's like, it's the real intimate moments

00:28:50.145 --> 00:28:51.471
that always stand out,

00:28:51.471 --> 00:28:53.255
and it's the real serene
moments that always stand out.

00:28:53.255 --> 00:28:56.114
And I think that's what
really sets "Berserk" apart

00:28:56.114 --> 00:28:57.813
from like so many other series

00:28:57.813 --> 00:28:59.877
where it's the serene moments juxtaposed

00:28:59.877 --> 00:29:02.069
against all like the horrific moments

00:29:02.069 --> 00:29:04.100
that make it one of, to me,

00:29:04.100 --> 00:29:07.067
like it's one of my
favorite pieces of fiction

00:29:07.067 --> 00:29:08.802
that's ever been made.

00:29:08.802 --> 00:29:12.440
I got reminded of that
after remembering everything

00:29:12.440 --> 00:29:14.573
that "Berserk" did.

00:29:14.573 --> 00:29:17.942
- It's like if the fucking
Doom guy had like a wife

00:29:17.942 --> 00:29:20.169
and family and he just
went home sometimes.

00:29:20.169 --> 00:29:21.257
(everyone laughs)

00:29:21.257 --> 00:29:23.956
You get reminded like,
"Oh shit, this is a guy."

00:29:23.956 --> 00:29:24.914
Because when you're-

00:29:24.914 --> 00:29:26.398
- Doom guy's like, "Why
am I killing these?"

00:29:26.398 --> 00:29:27.231
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:29:27.231 --> 00:29:28.064
"What is my purpose?"

00:29:28.064 --> 00:29:29.147
(everyone laughs)

00:29:29.147 --> 00:29:31.184
I was really, I, you know,

00:29:31.184 --> 00:29:33.142
'cause I don't know why
someone compared it on Twitter.

00:29:33.142 --> 00:29:35.847
I thought, I guess so,
but then I read "Berserk."

00:29:35.847 --> 00:29:38.205
I'm like, no, no, no.

00:29:38.205 --> 00:29:39.873
But it is kind of like, you do forget

00:29:39.873 --> 00:29:41.174
'cause sometimes like you're reading it,

00:29:41.174 --> 00:29:43.017
you're like, this is like so Doom-esque

00:29:43.017 --> 00:29:45.955
where he's just literally
just beheading horses.

00:29:45.955 --> 00:29:47.461
You're like, "Oh, this is like Doom."

00:29:47.461 --> 00:29:49.004
And then it's like really
sad and you're like,

00:29:49.004 --> 00:29:49.962
"This isn't like Doom."

00:29:49.962 --> 00:29:50.920
(everyone laughs)

00:29:50.920 --> 00:29:52.853
- It's literally that meme
where the girls were like,

00:29:52.853 --> 00:29:54.785
"I can't believe he
didn't cry during Titanic.

00:29:54.785 --> 00:29:56.400
"Do boys even have feelings?"

00:29:56.400 --> 00:29:59.735
And then like there's just the
boys crying over Guts' theme,

00:29:59.735 --> 00:30:02.037
which was literally what
I was doing that night.

00:30:02.037 --> 00:30:03.316
Just Guts' theme was playing

00:30:03.316 --> 00:30:04.886
and I was just like crying in bed.

00:30:04.886 --> 00:30:06.039
Just like, oh my God.

00:30:06.039 --> 00:30:07.477
- Yeah, I dunno.

00:30:07.477 --> 00:30:08.310
It's just, yeah.

00:30:08.310 --> 00:30:11.173
Like, every time I re-read it,
it's just because. you know,

00:30:11.173 --> 00:30:12.504
every time a new volume came out

00:30:12.504 --> 00:30:13.721
'cause it was so much time

00:30:13.721 --> 00:30:15.355
in between like the later volumes,

00:30:15.355 --> 00:30:16.978
I was like, "Well, fuck.

00:30:16.978 --> 00:30:18.322
"I guess I have to read
it from scratch again."

00:30:18.322 --> 00:30:20.267
And so I would keep reading
it from scratch over

00:30:20.267 --> 00:30:21.225
and over again.

00:30:21.225 --> 00:30:23.034
And it's one of those
shows where I'm just like,

00:30:23.034 --> 00:30:25.890
how does this not get like stale?

00:30:25.890 --> 00:30:28.942
Because I probably read it,
like the first 30 volumes,

00:30:28.942 --> 00:30:31.467
probably like a good,
like maybe 10, 20 times.

00:30:31.467 --> 00:30:34.064
I'm just like, how does this
keep just getting better?

00:30:34.064 --> 00:30:35.985
Like, how do I keep
finding new things in this?

00:30:35.985 --> 00:30:37.634
- I mean, you guys know me.

00:30:37.634 --> 00:30:38.663
I don't fucking rewatch anything.

00:30:38.663 --> 00:30:40.413
I refuse to rewatch.

00:30:40.413 --> 00:30:42.606
But even just rereading the first,

00:30:42.606 --> 00:30:43.747
what is the first one called?

00:30:43.747 --> 00:30:44.705
- "The Golden Age."

00:30:44.705 --> 00:30:45.538
- "The Golden Age," that.

00:30:45.538 --> 00:30:46.701
Just rereading that again, I'm like,

00:30:46.701 --> 00:30:48.154
"Holy shit, this was so good."

00:30:48.154 --> 00:30:48.987
- Yeah.

00:30:48.987 --> 00:30:51.618
- Like, even though I've seen
this, I've read it earlier.

00:30:51.618 --> 00:30:55.183
Like, I tried to read it again
ages ago for some reason now-

00:30:55.183 --> 00:30:56.136
- Sometimes when I'm bored,

00:30:56.136 --> 00:30:58.587
I just like go to the eclipse
arc and just look at the art.

00:30:58.587 --> 00:30:59.420
- Yeah.

00:30:59.420 --> 00:31:02.334
- I'm like, how can one
person think of this?

00:31:02.334 --> 00:31:03.167
- Yeah, I know.

00:31:03.167 --> 00:31:04.125
- It's just insane.

00:31:04.125 --> 00:31:05.204
- And you know-

00:31:05.204 --> 00:31:06.623
- And the dude was like 15 as well

00:31:06.623 --> 00:31:08.920
when he like first came up
with the concept of the zone.

00:31:08.920 --> 00:31:11.738
- Did you see the manga
he made before "Berserk"

00:31:11.738 --> 00:31:13.787
when he was actually 15?
- He was like 15 or 16.

00:31:13.787 --> 00:31:16.521
- It's better than most
modern manga artists.

00:31:16.521 --> 00:31:19.562
- I'm like, this is not the
art skill of a 15-year-old.

00:31:19.562 --> 00:31:20.395
- Exactly, exactly.

00:31:20.395 --> 00:31:22.436
And like he paired that talent

00:31:22.436 --> 00:31:25.676
and he just kept improving
on it to the point

00:31:25.676 --> 00:31:29.251
where literally, I dunno,
there's only like a few people

00:31:29.251 --> 00:31:31.667
in the world who I think
can even match, you know,

00:31:31.667 --> 00:31:34.167
the talent that he puts
into the panels that he did.

00:31:34.167 --> 00:31:36.233
- I mean, I saw this like
really interesting interview

00:31:36.233 --> 00:31:39.087
with him like after, you
know, his death was announced

00:31:39.087 --> 00:31:41.712
where like apparently
one of the big reasons

00:31:41.712 --> 00:31:45.394
as to why he was on hiatus was
because he got so infatuated

00:31:45.394 --> 00:31:48.550
with detail that it would
literally get to the point

00:31:48.550 --> 00:31:50.180
where he would zoom in

00:31:50.180 --> 00:31:53.640
and like actually edit
every fucking pixel.

00:31:53.640 --> 00:31:54.777
- [Garnt] Yeah.

00:31:54.777 --> 00:31:55.610
- Oh my God.

00:31:55.610 --> 00:31:56.443
- And like he-

00:31:56.443 --> 00:31:57.852
- Sounds like a prison, that's perfection.

00:31:57.852 --> 00:31:59.302
- Yeah, and he kept, you know,

00:31:59.302 --> 00:32:01.467
getting like on hiatus
over and over again.

00:32:01.467 --> 00:32:03.528
And his, you know, editors would be like,

00:32:03.528 --> 00:32:05.629
"You can't even see this detail on paper.

00:32:05.629 --> 00:32:06.552
"So like just stop."

00:32:06.552 --> 00:32:07.979
And he was just like, "No.

00:32:07.979 --> 00:32:08.937
"I have to get this right.

00:32:08.937 --> 00:32:09.895
"I have to get this perfect."

00:32:09.895 --> 00:32:12.996
- Honestly, like some of
the panels he's done belongs

00:32:12.996 --> 00:32:14.212
in a museum, you know?

00:32:14.212 --> 00:32:17.089
'Cause like the reason for that is

00:32:17.089 --> 00:32:19.654
'cause I just remember like
that night when I went back,

00:32:19.654 --> 00:32:21.941
I just like went to look
at some of the panels

00:32:21.941 --> 00:32:24.271
and I just remember staring
at them for such a long time

00:32:24.271 --> 00:32:25.988
because you know when
you're reading a story,

00:32:25.988 --> 00:32:29.568
sometimes, you know, you
wanna see what happens next.

00:32:29.568 --> 00:32:30.401
So you don't read it.

00:32:30.401 --> 00:32:33.620
You don't appreciate the art at the moment

00:32:33.620 --> 00:32:35.358
when you first read it.

00:32:35.358 --> 00:32:37.550
But I went back to look
at some of the panels,

00:32:37.550 --> 00:32:40.714
and I just, the amount of
work and amount of detail

00:32:40.714 --> 00:32:42.378
and the amount of vision that was put

00:32:42.378 --> 00:32:45.040
into these panels were fucking amazing.

00:32:45.040 --> 00:32:47.649
I did not appreciate
it fully the first time

00:32:47.649 --> 00:32:49.699
even though I could
tell these were amazing.

00:32:49.699 --> 00:32:51.342
I didn't take the time to fully appreciate

00:32:51.342 --> 00:32:54.210
how fucking amazing
some of these panels are

00:32:54.210 --> 00:32:55.698
'cause they are incredible.

00:32:55.698 --> 00:32:56.562
- [Joey] 100%.

00:32:56.562 --> 00:32:59.789
- They, you know, they are
just basically the same

00:32:59.789 --> 00:33:01.576
as any other painting or any other art.

00:33:01.576 --> 00:33:03.269
- I really want to know if they have

00:33:03.269 --> 00:33:05.389
like a "Berserk" art book of some kind

00:33:05.389 --> 00:33:08.026
because I would fucking purchase
that in a heartbeat, dude.

00:33:08.026 --> 00:33:09.327
- I can imagine

00:33:09.327 --> 00:33:11.382
that they'll probably end
up doing something soon

00:33:11.382 --> 00:33:13.278
to celebrate the legacy.

00:33:13.278 --> 00:33:16.339
- I hope they do like open
up an exhibit or something.

00:33:16.339 --> 00:33:18.400
'Cause that would be absolutely amazing

00:33:18.400 --> 00:33:20.928
'cause if there's one, you know, one manga

00:33:20.928 --> 00:33:22.144
that deserves an exhibit,

00:33:22.144 --> 00:33:24.509
that deserves the artwork
to be plastered on the wall.

00:33:24.509 --> 00:33:25.384
- It's Miura, yeah.

00:33:25.384 --> 00:33:26.217
- It's fucking "Berserk."

00:33:26.217 --> 00:33:27.175
- Yeah, 100%.

00:33:27.175 --> 00:33:28.836
- It was kind of sad to see
that a lot of people were

00:33:28.836 --> 00:33:30.489
just like, "Well, what's
gonna happen to the story?"

00:33:30.489 --> 00:33:31.447
And it's like-

00:33:31.447 --> 00:33:33.354
- Those aren't fans of "Berserk."

00:33:33.354 --> 00:33:34.187
- It's frustrating

00:33:34.187 --> 00:33:35.641
'cause when I saw the
announcement on Twitter

00:33:35.641 --> 00:33:36.644
there were so many people being like,

00:33:36.644 --> 00:33:37.869
"Does this mean it's not gonna finish?"

00:33:37.869 --> 00:33:39.805
- It's like, yes, no shit.

00:33:39.805 --> 00:33:41.187
- To me, it's just so, it's like,

00:33:41.187 --> 00:33:42.978
how about you just give
them a chance to like grieve

00:33:42.978 --> 00:33:44.633
before you ask these questions.

00:33:44.633 --> 00:33:45.884
- If anything I'm kind of-

00:33:45.884 --> 00:33:47.322
- The answer's probably gonna be no.

00:33:47.322 --> 00:33:49.222
- Because there were a lot
of people as well being like,

00:33:49.222 --> 00:33:50.055
"Oh, but you know,

00:33:50.055 --> 00:33:51.801
"they can probably just
get like Miura's assistants

00:33:51.801 --> 00:33:52.634
"to finish it."

00:33:52.634 --> 00:33:53.717
And like, no, no.

00:33:53.717 --> 00:33:55.939
I would rather it just be where it is.

00:33:55.939 --> 00:33:56.772
Just end it.

00:33:56.772 --> 00:33:59.656
- I'm fine with it being
an unfinished masterpiece,

00:33:59.656 --> 00:34:00.489
you know?

00:34:00.489 --> 00:34:01.322
That's fine.

00:34:01.322 --> 00:34:02.421
That's fine for me.

00:34:02.421 --> 00:34:03.422
It's "Berserk"-

00:34:03.422 --> 00:34:06.523
- Was it realistically ever
gonna finish, do you think?

00:34:06.523 --> 00:34:08.486
- I mean, I don't think,

00:34:08.486 --> 00:34:11.162
like, not a single one
of like the, you know,

00:34:11.162 --> 00:34:12.605
the Kings were killed.

00:34:12.605 --> 00:34:13.994
I think only one of them was killed.

00:34:13.994 --> 00:34:14.863
- [Garnt] I think one of them was.

00:34:14.863 --> 00:34:15.821
- Yeah, yeah.

00:34:15.821 --> 00:34:18.324
So, there was a long, long way to go.

00:34:18.324 --> 00:34:20.844
- We were so early in the story

00:34:20.844 --> 00:34:23.775
and the pace that the
story was progressing,

00:34:23.775 --> 00:34:26.689
I doubt it would have finished
in our lifetime or, you know,

00:34:26.689 --> 00:34:28.919
I think it was always
going to be unfinished.

00:34:28.919 --> 00:34:32.237
But I think "Berserk" has
already achieved enough

00:34:32.237 --> 00:34:34.598
that it doesn't need to be finished.

00:34:34.598 --> 00:34:36.307
- Yeah, it was like what I said

00:34:36.307 --> 00:34:38.693
when we talked about last time
we spoke about reading manga

00:34:38.693 --> 00:34:40.035
where I just get to,

00:34:40.035 --> 00:34:42.405
I often get to a point when
I'm reading manga I'm like,

00:34:42.405 --> 00:34:43.363
"I'm satisfied.

00:34:43.363 --> 00:34:46.671
"I genuinely, it'd be
cool if this ends nicely,

00:34:46.671 --> 00:34:47.752
"but I've read up to a point

00:34:47.752 --> 00:34:50.301
"where I feel like I'm happy
with what I've been given."

00:34:50.301 --> 00:34:53.040
And I feel like "Berserk"
has definitely done that.

00:34:53.040 --> 00:34:55.265
- There's been plenty
of moments in "Berserk"

00:34:55.265 --> 00:34:58.385
that have felt like a resolution moment,

00:34:58.385 --> 00:34:59.655
like a big resolution moment.

00:34:59.655 --> 00:35:02.026
Even though not every
plot detail was resolved,

00:35:02.026 --> 00:35:04.409
even though not every
loose end was tied up,

00:35:04.409 --> 00:35:07.654
I feel like it's resolved
enough in my heart

00:35:07.654 --> 00:35:11.368
to make it like impact me
this much already, you know?

00:35:11.368 --> 00:35:14.356
And I think "Berserk," you know,

00:35:14.356 --> 00:35:17.176
the journey of Guts is already
amazing enough as it is.

00:35:17.176 --> 00:35:18.661
And some journeys, you know,

00:35:18.661 --> 00:35:21.304
some journeys don't need
to come to an end on paper,

00:35:21.304 --> 00:35:22.762
you know?

00:35:22.762 --> 00:35:25.418
I've seen enough of the
journey where I'm satisfied.

00:35:25.418 --> 00:35:26.848
It's...

00:35:26.848 --> 00:35:29.265
- Just knowing that he's
out there somewhere still.

00:35:29.265 --> 00:35:30.672
Looking for the end, right?

00:35:30.672 --> 00:35:31.630
- Exactly.

00:35:31.630 --> 00:35:32.729
- With the biggest fucking sword.

00:35:32.729 --> 00:35:34.142
(everyone laughs)

00:35:34.142 --> 00:35:36.475
- Fat fucking sword.

00:35:36.475 --> 00:35:38.442
- Yeah, honestly I don't
know what else to say.

00:35:38.442 --> 00:35:41.834
It was just, it's a story
that has impacted me.

00:35:41.834 --> 00:35:43.087
- If there's anything we can say

00:35:43.087 --> 00:35:44.505
on this "Trash Taste" episode,

00:35:44.505 --> 00:35:46.284
it's please go read "Berserk."

00:35:46.284 --> 00:35:47.242
Give it a go.

00:35:47.242 --> 00:35:48.180
- Pay respect to the king.

00:35:48.180 --> 00:35:49.013
- Yeah.

00:35:49.013 --> 00:35:49.846
- Honestly.

00:35:49.846 --> 00:35:51.259
- Honestly, he is a king.

00:35:51.259 --> 00:35:52.929
- He's the fucking GOAT, man.

00:35:52.929 --> 00:35:57.322
- I hope, you know, if we find
out more about the details

00:35:57.322 --> 00:36:01.574
of, you know, what might've
caused his early death,

00:36:01.574 --> 00:36:03.948
that if it is something to
do with being overworked

00:36:03.948 --> 00:36:05.159
or anything, the lifestyle,

00:36:05.159 --> 00:36:07.204
that I hope it does
make a change, if it is.

00:36:07.204 --> 00:36:08.190
We don't know that, obviously.

00:36:08.190 --> 00:36:09.421
We might never know.

00:36:09.421 --> 00:36:10.846
But if we do find out more details,

00:36:10.846 --> 00:36:13.203
and it becomes publicly
available, and we, you know,

00:36:13.203 --> 00:36:15.612
we know that maybe being overworked is-

00:36:15.612 --> 00:36:17.467
- Yeah, I think it would be
good to at least, you know,

00:36:17.467 --> 00:36:19.174
kind of put into the public discussion.

00:36:19.174 --> 00:36:22.284
- Because, you know, even if you are,

00:36:22.284 --> 00:36:24.652
you know, you have, 'cause
normally with heart problems

00:36:24.652 --> 00:36:25.822
and this kind of blood stuff,

00:36:25.822 --> 00:36:28.117
it's normally there is some
hereditary stuff at play.

00:36:28.117 --> 00:36:30.014
But I mean still at 54 is young.

00:36:30.014 --> 00:36:31.097
Like, that...

00:36:31.097 --> 00:36:33.598
Lifestyle would have to have an effect.

00:36:33.598 --> 00:36:34.431
- I think so.

00:36:34.431 --> 00:36:38.485
- I just want mangas to
not have so much stress

00:36:38.485 --> 00:36:40.858
on their body where it fails, you know?

00:36:40.858 --> 00:36:41.691
I don't know.

00:36:41.691 --> 00:36:42.649
I feel bad, man.

00:36:42.649 --> 00:36:43.482
It makes me feel shitty.

00:36:43.482 --> 00:36:47.499
- Yeah, I mean, it sucks
because like, you know,

00:36:47.499 --> 00:36:49.352
there's not really much I can add to that

00:36:49.352 --> 00:36:51.883
because manga artists work a hell of a-

00:36:51.883 --> 00:36:52.716
- We know, we know-

00:36:52.716 --> 00:36:54.205
- We know they work way too hard.

00:36:54.205 --> 00:36:55.213
- Whether voluntarily or not,

00:36:55.213 --> 00:36:56.656
the deadlines that they set themselves

00:36:56.656 --> 00:36:59.402
or are set on them are too much.

00:36:59.402 --> 00:37:02.272
And it doesn't help that
fans are so demanding.

00:37:02.272 --> 00:37:03.381
And that for some fucking reason,

00:37:03.381 --> 00:37:05.246
the first question that some fans have

00:37:05.246 --> 00:37:06.857
when an author dies is
what happens to the story.

00:37:06.857 --> 00:37:10.263
It's like, I mean, it feels so selfish,

00:37:10.263 --> 00:37:11.378
and it feels, you know,

00:37:11.378 --> 00:37:15.025
because we as fans also have
something where we're selfish.

00:37:15.025 --> 00:37:16.108
- Yeah, yeah.

00:37:16.108 --> 00:37:18.955
I don't know, like
surprisingly, from what I saw,

00:37:18.955 --> 00:37:21.114
there weren't as many of those comments.

00:37:21.114 --> 00:37:22.072
- It wasn't that bad.

00:37:22.072 --> 00:37:24.681
It just sours your taste
when you see even one.

00:37:24.681 --> 00:37:26.674
- Every now and then
I saw it and I'm like,

00:37:26.674 --> 00:37:28.542
"Okay, clearly you don't
really give a shit."

00:37:28.542 --> 00:37:32.367
- I mean, none of them said offensive.

00:37:32.367 --> 00:37:35.301
- There were just some
of the insensitive ones.

00:37:35.301 --> 00:37:36.944
- It reminds me of a-

00:37:36.944 --> 00:37:39.018
- But it's like when there's
earthquakes and stuff, right,

00:37:39.018 --> 00:37:40.358
but people are always just like,

00:37:40.358 --> 00:37:43.488
"Oh, the manga it's delayed
'cause of an earthquake?"

00:37:43.488 --> 00:37:45.606
And it's like, what do you mean?

00:37:45.606 --> 00:37:48.475
Like, people like people die.

00:37:48.475 --> 00:37:49.683
- Exactly.

00:37:49.683 --> 00:37:51.720
- Like, earthquakes are no fucking joke.

00:37:51.720 --> 00:37:54.126
And it's like the people
that most, I mean, you know,

00:37:54.126 --> 00:37:55.908
obviously with this situation
is very sensitive, you know,

00:37:55.908 --> 00:37:58.131
and it was very fresh
and a lot of people care.

00:37:58.131 --> 00:38:00.581
But I noticed, especially with
like earthquakes and stuff,

00:38:00.581 --> 00:38:02.717
that people are very quick to be like,

00:38:02.717 --> 00:38:03.594
"Oh, who gives a shit?

00:38:03.594 --> 00:38:04.598
"It's just an earthquake."

00:38:04.598 --> 00:38:05.806
- "It happens all the time."

00:38:05.806 --> 00:38:06.639
- And it's like,

00:38:06.639 --> 00:38:10.234
I think it plays into
the overall sentiment

00:38:10.234 --> 00:38:11.438
of that a lot of anime fans

00:38:11.438 --> 00:38:13.424
and manga fans are very
demanding for the stuff

00:38:13.424 --> 00:38:14.308
that they want.

00:38:14.308 --> 00:38:17.383
And I feel like we as fans
need to chill out a little bit.

00:38:17.383 --> 00:38:19.332
- Yeah, they care about the product,

00:38:19.332 --> 00:38:21.109
but not so much about
the person making it.

00:38:21.109 --> 00:38:23.066
- Yeah, I feel like we as fans
generally need to chill out

00:38:23.066 --> 00:38:26.094
about our passion for anime and manga.

00:38:26.094 --> 00:38:26.927
- I'd say that.

00:38:26.927 --> 00:38:27.760
- External things happen.

00:38:27.760 --> 00:38:28.593
They happen.

00:38:28.593 --> 00:38:29.551
It is what it is.

00:38:29.551 --> 00:38:32.169
- Remember that some actual
person is making your product.

00:38:32.169 --> 00:38:34.348
- Whether it be an earthquake
or personal stress,

00:38:34.348 --> 00:38:36.521
they're all valid reasons
for work to be delayed.

00:38:36.521 --> 00:38:37.479
- Give them some respect.

00:38:37.479 --> 00:38:40.417
- I just want creators to
be able to create the shit

00:38:40.417 --> 00:38:43.508
to the best of their ability
and not have to worry.

00:38:43.508 --> 00:38:45.572
I hope that's not
controversial for me to say.

00:38:45.572 --> 00:38:47.280
- What a hot take!

00:38:47.280 --> 00:38:48.488
- I don't know.

00:38:48.488 --> 00:38:50.263
- Respect staff members.

00:38:50.263 --> 00:38:52.548
- I don't know, I just feel
like when you say this shit-

00:38:52.548 --> 00:38:53.863
- There's people behind the work.

00:38:53.863 --> 00:38:56.700
I mean, I'm sure everyone can agree on it.

00:38:56.700 --> 00:38:58.020
It's just more, you know,

00:38:58.020 --> 00:39:02.046
I'm sure 99% of people
watching this don't do that.

00:39:02.046 --> 00:39:03.332
It's just that 1%.

00:39:03.332 --> 00:39:04.379
It's always that 1%.

00:39:04.379 --> 00:39:05.212
'Cause I remember,

00:39:05.212 --> 00:39:07.173
this reminds me of like
the "Game of Thrones" thing

00:39:07.173 --> 00:39:11.219
with JRR Martin where I remember
like seeing an interview

00:39:11.219 --> 00:39:13.756
with him and he said that he got annoyed

00:39:13.756 --> 00:39:16.462
that some people were
worried about his health

00:39:16.462 --> 00:39:18.118
not because they were
worried about his health,

00:39:18.118 --> 00:39:20.150
but they're worried if he would be alive

00:39:20.150 --> 00:39:21.887
to finish "Game of Thrones."

00:39:21.887 --> 00:39:23.715
And I'm just like, yeah,
that's pretty fucked up

00:39:23.715 --> 00:39:26.739
that like fans are saying
that to you, aren't they.

00:39:26.739 --> 00:39:27.768
- Jesus Christ.

00:39:27.768 --> 00:39:28.867
- And even if they didn't say it,

00:39:28.867 --> 00:39:31.033
I'm sure he knows that people
are probably thinking it.

00:39:31.033 --> 00:39:33.116
- Yeah, he can read between the lines.

00:39:33.116 --> 00:39:35.066
- People only care about his well-being

00:39:35.066 --> 00:39:36.151
in terms of the book.

00:39:36.151 --> 00:39:38.784
Like, he's being fucking
held hostage by the story.

00:39:38.784 --> 00:39:39.784
Like, you know what I mean?

00:39:39.784 --> 00:39:40.799
You can't fucking do anything.

00:39:40.799 --> 00:39:43.376
- If anyone knows the intention
of "Game of Thrones" fans,

00:39:43.376 --> 00:39:45.131
it's the guy who made "Game of Thrones."

00:39:45.131 --> 00:39:46.412
(everyone laughs)

00:39:46.412 --> 00:39:47.595
- It's just sad, it's just sad.

00:39:47.595 --> 00:39:48.428
I don't know.

00:39:48.428 --> 00:39:50.609
Like, this makes me sad for
like many reasons, you know?

00:39:50.609 --> 00:39:52.207
There's just so much at play.

00:39:52.207 --> 00:39:55.376
- This is well, I mean, it's
a sad topic unfortunately.

00:39:55.376 --> 00:39:56.374
- It's all about the respect.

00:39:56.374 --> 00:39:57.207
That's all it is.

00:39:57.207 --> 00:39:59.592
Respect the creators, respect the artists.

00:39:59.592 --> 00:40:01.412
Give them some space
if they're feeling sick

00:40:01.412 --> 00:40:02.245
or need a break.

00:40:02.245 --> 00:40:03.328
- Yeah.

00:40:03.328 --> 00:40:05.878
Moving on to lighter topics though.

00:40:05.878 --> 00:40:08.589
I heard you've been watching
anime recently, Connor.

00:40:08.589 --> 00:40:09.422
- Kinda yeah.

00:40:09.422 --> 00:40:11.339
- Which is a rare feat.

00:40:12.877 --> 00:40:14.507
- I remember I used to do that.

00:40:14.507 --> 00:40:15.543
(everyone laughs)

00:40:15.543 --> 00:40:16.626
- The anime man.

00:40:16.626 --> 00:40:17.459
What happened?

00:40:17.459 --> 00:40:19.593
- Did you guys watch
"Castlevania," the new season?

00:40:19.593 --> 00:40:21.020
- I have not.
- Not season four.

00:40:21.020 --> 00:40:21.853
- Bro, it's so-

00:40:21.853 --> 00:40:23.179
- But we haven't talked about
"Castlevania" yet, have we?

00:40:23.179 --> 00:40:24.601
- It's so good, it's so good.

00:40:24.601 --> 00:40:25.509
- I mean with how,

00:40:25.509 --> 00:40:27.367
I mean, I've watched up to season three.

00:40:27.367 --> 00:40:30.459
If there's one anime I have
like kind of caught up to,

00:40:30.459 --> 00:40:31.542
it's "Castlevania."

00:40:31.542 --> 00:40:32.375
But like-

00:40:32.375 --> 00:40:33.234
- Where did you get up
to in "Castlevania?"

00:40:33.234 --> 00:40:35.396
- I got up to season three.

00:40:35.396 --> 00:40:36.641
So, I haven't finished season three.

00:40:36.641 --> 00:40:39.274
I'm about halfway through season three.

00:40:39.274 --> 00:40:41.379
But I mean, it's just been for me,

00:40:41.379 --> 00:40:43.006
it's been getting better
and better every season

00:40:43.006 --> 00:40:44.141
as it's been going on

00:40:44.141 --> 00:40:45.788
and I just haven't had
time to binge it yet.

00:40:45.788 --> 00:40:46.621
So...

00:40:47.496 --> 00:40:48.329
- I don't know, man.

00:40:48.329 --> 00:40:50.284
Everything about that anime,
especially the past season,

00:40:50.284 --> 00:40:51.396
just blew it out the water.

00:40:51.396 --> 00:40:52.354
- What's so good about it?

00:40:52.354 --> 00:40:53.850
- Like, I feel like
everything that was good

00:40:53.850 --> 00:40:55.934
in previous seasons was
at its best this season.

00:40:55.934 --> 00:40:56.767
- Really?

00:40:56.767 --> 00:40:57.850
- The story was the best.

00:40:57.850 --> 00:40:59.917
The animation was just insane.

00:40:59.917 --> 00:41:00.750
Like, some of the fights.

00:41:00.750 --> 00:41:01.952
Even though in season three,

00:41:01.952 --> 00:41:04.082
the fights like the
final fight was so good.

00:41:04.082 --> 00:41:05.721
- Even season one had
some crazy animation.

00:41:05.721 --> 00:41:07.178
- It just feels like
they've stepped it up.

00:41:07.178 --> 00:41:09.648
Like again, like I think
one of the strongest points

00:41:09.648 --> 00:41:11.681
of "Castlevania" has
been the voice acting.

00:41:11.681 --> 00:41:13.109
The English voice acting-

00:41:13.109 --> 00:41:14.628
- The English voice acting is fantastic.

00:41:14.628 --> 00:41:15.586
- Insane.

00:41:15.586 --> 00:41:16.561
- It's fantastic.

00:41:16.561 --> 00:41:19.590
- Like, the fact that they
have like all the accents

00:41:19.590 --> 00:41:22.055
on point, none of the accents feel silly.

