Every single accent
that the characters have

00:41:23.370 --> 00:41:24.499
it feels genuine.

00:41:24.499 --> 00:41:26.317
Every single British accent is on point.

00:41:26.317 --> 00:41:27.817
And it's like, holy shit.

00:41:27.817 --> 00:41:28.775
How do they do this?

00:41:28.775 --> 00:41:30.191
This never happens in anime.

00:41:30.191 --> 00:41:31.767
How did they get an actual accent?

00:41:31.767 --> 00:41:34.198
- It's like they hired British actors.

00:41:34.198 --> 00:41:36.161
- I love the fact that
for example the JoJo

00:41:36.161 --> 00:41:38.459
in the dub like tried to do the accent,

00:41:38.459 --> 00:41:40.808
but I wish they'd got the native people.

00:41:40.808 --> 00:41:41.674
- Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:41:41.674 --> 00:41:42.564
- Because like in "JoJo Part One,"

00:41:42.564 --> 00:41:45.198
it's Johnny Yong Bosch
doing in a British accent,

00:41:45.198 --> 00:41:46.281
which isn't bad.
- Yeah, it is.

00:41:46.281 --> 00:41:47.364
- Which isn't bad.

00:41:47.364 --> 00:41:50.018
But I know there's no
shortage of native English,

00:41:50.018 --> 00:41:52.881
British accents that can work in LA.

00:41:52.881 --> 00:41:54.548
You know, like...

00:41:54.548 --> 00:41:56.938
- It feels like the
voice actors they hired

00:41:56.938 --> 00:41:58.797
for "Castlevania" were
just outside of your

00:41:58.797 --> 00:42:00.114
usual anime voice actors.

00:42:00.114 --> 00:42:01.330
- They were just general actors.

00:42:01.330 --> 00:42:03.176
- Yeah, they felt like general actors

00:42:03.176 --> 00:42:04.903
that would act in like a TV series

00:42:04.903 --> 00:42:06.106
or like a live action movie.

00:42:06.106 --> 00:42:07.261
