00:57:55.041 --> 00:57:56.255
they were like, "No, no.

00:57:56.255 --> 00:57:58.688
"We think we could improve
this for an English audience."

00:57:58.688 --> 00:58:00.305
Which is a bold thing to do, you know?

00:58:00.305 --> 00:58:01.765
And we've had a lot of failures.

00:58:01.765 --> 00:58:05.132
We've had a lot of things
that have gone wrong.

00:58:05.132 --> 00:58:05.990
- A lot of questionable ones.

00:58:05.990 --> 00:58:07.765
- But I do really appreciate
when it's done right.

00:58:07.765 --> 00:58:10.168
And I appreciate it more so
than a attempted translation

00:58:10.168 --> 00:58:13.008
'cause I feel like the
actors have a way harder time

00:58:13.008 --> 00:58:14.868
delivering Japanese dialogue essentially.

00:58:14.868 --> 00:58:15.808
I mean, that's what that is.

00:58:15.808 --> 00:58:17.801
- Because it's really hard to also perform

00:58:17.801 --> 00:58:20.941
directly translated to Japanese dialogue

00:58:20.941 --> 00:58:22.691
to make it sound natural in English

00:58:22.691 --> 00:58:24.322
because there's just some
times where it's like,

00:58:24.322 --> 00:58:26.147
that doesn't sound like
something someone would say

00:58:26.147 --> 00:58:27.822
in English, you know?

00:58:27.822 --> 00:58:30.687
Like, I especially felt that more when I,

00:58:30.687 --> 00:58:32.759
'cause like when I did like
a bit of translation work

00:58:32.759 --> 00:58:34.419
during like school and stuff like that,

00:58:34.419 --> 00:58:36.150
and I like learned linguistics and stuff.

00:58:36.150 --> 00:58:37.450
Like, that's where I was like,

00:58:37.450 --> 00:58:40.065
because I also used to be
like, "How hard could it be?

00:58:40.065 --> 00:58:41.766
"Just like direct translate it, you know,

00:58:41.766 --> 00:58:43.047
"to get the meaning across."

00:58:43.047 --> 00:58:45.055
But then when I actually started doing it,

00:58:45.055 --> 00:58:47.243
I was like, "Oh no, you just can't."

00:58:47.243 --> 00:58:48.618
Like, it's not a matter of like preference

00:58:48.618 --> 00:58:49.468
or anything like that.

00:58:49.468 --> 00:58:51.237
It's just like you physically can't.

00:58:51.237 --> 00:58:53.326
There were just some Japanese
like ways of saying things

00:58:53.326 --> 00:58:55.691
that where you just like, if
I did directly translate it,

00:58:55.691 --> 00:58:58.978
it would just be a bunch of
words that don't mean anything.

00:58:58.978 --> 00:59:01.335
- I think, 'cause I don't know if,

00:59:01.335 --> 00:59:05.299
even though I spoke two
languages from birth,

00:59:05.299 --> 00:59:07.607
I always thought as languages as like,

00:59:07.607 --> 00:59:09.676
they're all just the same thing

00:59:09.676 --> 00:59:11.591
just said in different ways.

00:59:11.591 --> 00:59:13.398
But then like if that makes sense

00:59:13.398 --> 00:59:15.138
where everything can be
one-to-one translated.

00:59:15.138 --> 00:59:16.911
- No, no, I get what you mean.

00:59:16.911 --> 00:59:18.944
- Every meaning can be
expressed in another language.

00:59:18.944 --> 00:59:19.851
- Yeah, absolutely.

00:59:19.851 --> 00:59:22.429
- I think 'cause we've been
spoiled 'cause things have been,

00:59:22.429 --> 00:59:24.387
our whole life we've just had things

00:59:24.387 --> 00:59:25.872
that have been translated.

00:59:25.872 --> 00:59:27.814
- So we've never known what
the other side is like.

00:59:27.814 --> 00:59:29.257
- It's English, it's
been translated for us.

00:59:29.257 --> 00:59:31.706
And even again, even though
I spoke two languages,

00:59:31.706 --> 00:59:33.423
I could never wrap my
head around this concept

00:59:33.423 --> 00:59:34.995
until I started learning Japanese

00:59:34.995 --> 00:59:37.812
where I was like, oh, it's just like,

00:59:37.812 --> 00:59:39.531
it's like another planet

00:59:39.531 --> 00:59:41.589
where it hasn't even touched anything.

00:59:41.589 --> 00:59:43.955
I don't know how to
describe this like mental-

00:59:43.955 --> 00:59:45.265
- It's so hard to describe

00:59:45.265 --> 00:59:46.929
for someone who only speaks one language.

00:59:46.929 --> 00:59:49.852
'Cause I remember the first
time I noticed this was

00:59:49.852 --> 00:59:52.492
I was watching a Thai film with Sydney,

00:59:52.492 --> 00:59:55.320
and I, you know, she obviously
had English subtitles on,

00:59:55.320 --> 00:59:58.552
and as someone who speaks both
Thai and can read English,

00:59:58.552 --> 00:59:59.770
it was really distracting;

00:59:59.770 --> 01:00:03.392
one, because it felt like
I was hearing something

01:00:03.392 --> 01:00:06.582
and seeing something and they
both meant the same thing

01:00:06.582 --> 01:00:08.412
but they felt different for me.

01:00:08.412 --> 01:00:12.850
It's this language dissonance
that I can't quite describe.

01:00:12.850 --> 01:00:16.650
But it's something that I
feel like having now trying

01:00:16.650 --> 01:00:17.733
to learn the language that, you know,

01:00:17.733 --> 01:00:22.482
part of a culture and part
of like an entire country's,

01:00:22.482 --> 01:00:25.843
you know, way of thinking
and culture is just ingrained

01:00:25.843 --> 01:00:26.712
into a language.

01:00:26.712 --> 01:00:28.987
It's just so much deeper than just,

01:00:28.987 --> 01:00:30.855
I say one thing, it means another thing.

01:00:30.855 --> 01:00:34.451
Like, I would say that depending
on what language I speak,

01:00:34.451 --> 01:00:36.382
my personality kind of shifts as well

01:00:36.382 --> 01:00:39.684
because it's a different
kind of way of thinking

01:00:39.684 --> 01:00:41.598
when you're speaking another language.

01:00:41.598 --> 01:00:44.041
It's so hard to describe

01:00:44.041 --> 01:00:46.255
for anyone who only speaks one language,

01:00:46.255 --> 01:00:48.572
but anyone who does
speak two languages will

01:00:48.572 --> 01:00:50.498
probably understand that you probably have

01:00:50.498 --> 01:00:52.754
a slightly different personality
speaking one language

01:00:52.754 --> 01:00:53.784
compared to another.

01:00:53.784 --> 01:00:56.223
- I apparently have a
completely different personality

01:00:56.223 --> 01:00:58.093
when I speak Japanese compared to English.

01:00:58.093 --> 01:00:59.387
- You're a lot softer.

01:00:59.387 --> 01:01:01.338
- Yeah, you're a lot softer.
- What in English or Japanese?

01:01:01.338 --> 01:01:02.171
- Japanese.
- Japanese.

01:01:02.171 --> 01:01:03.004
- Really?

01:01:03.004 --> 01:01:03.837
- I think so.

01:01:03.837 --> 01:01:04.795
- I always thought it was the opposite.

01:01:04.795 --> 01:01:05.762
- Maybe, I don't know.

01:01:05.762 --> 01:01:06.878
I think that's just surface level.

01:01:06.878 --> 01:01:07.711
I don't know.

01:01:07.711 --> 01:01:08.544
- Yeah.

01:01:08.544 --> 01:01:10.409
- But like I also realized as well,

01:01:10.409 --> 01:01:12.078
'cause, you know, sometimes
you're in class or whatever,

01:01:12.078 --> 01:01:14.453
you're asking, "Oh, how do
I say this in Japanese?"

01:01:14.453 --> 01:01:15.932
Like, no, you can't say that Japanese.

01:01:15.932 --> 01:01:17.067
It doesn't exist in Japanese.

01:01:17.067 --> 01:01:17.900
It's not a concept.

01:01:17.900 --> 01:01:19.313
They've never thought of that.

01:01:19.313 --> 01:01:20.359
- Yeah, oh God, you just fucking,

01:01:20.359 --> 01:01:22.271
like flashback to me in school.

01:01:22.271 --> 01:01:27.168
Everyone being like, "How do
you say fuck in Japanese?"

01:01:27.168 --> 01:01:29.817
I'm like, how do I explain
that doesn't exist?

01:01:29.817 --> 01:01:32.425
- And then I realized
because Welsh and English,

01:01:32.425 --> 01:01:36.135
because although they are
entirely different languages,

01:01:36.135 --> 01:01:36.968
everyone thinks,

01:01:36.968 --> 01:01:38.891
"Oh, well Welsh is just
another version of English."

01:01:38.891 --> 01:01:40.594
It's like completely different.

01:01:40.594 --> 01:01:41.462
It's, you know-

01:01:41.462 --> 01:01:42.478
- But you're in the UK.

01:01:42.478 --> 01:01:43.311
You're in the same country.

01:01:43.311 --> 01:01:46.756
- Like, German is closer
to English than Welsh is.

01:01:46.756 --> 01:01:49.339
And it's the reason why I think

01:01:50.525 --> 01:01:52.369
that I never had this
realization before was

01:01:52.369 --> 01:01:54.889
because it's the culture
that you grew up in.

01:01:54.889 --> 01:01:56.989
Because the countries
have a similar culture

01:01:56.989 --> 01:01:58.985
now at least in the modern day.

01:01:58.985 --> 01:02:01.196
The concepts do sort of translate

01:02:01.196 --> 01:02:03.118
because we've made them translate.

01:02:03.118 --> 01:02:05.072
Like, we've made the concept felt by both.

01:02:05.072 --> 01:02:05.913
And so that-

01:02:05.913 --> 01:02:07.768
- There isn't like the cultural gap.

01:02:07.768 --> 01:02:08.601
- Right, right.

01:02:08.601 --> 01:02:09.820
Because the cultural
gap is like inherently,

01:02:09.820 --> 01:02:11.707
there's just sayings and stuff

01:02:11.707 --> 01:02:13.383
that will never, ever have a meaning

01:02:13.383 --> 01:02:15.286
no matter how much you
try and translate them

01:02:15.286 --> 01:02:16.240
'cause it's just an inherent,

01:02:16.240 --> 01:02:17.916
it's a feeling. And it's a, I don't know.

01:02:17.916 --> 01:02:19.681
This is just a weird concept
that we're going down,

01:02:19.681 --> 01:02:21.204
and it seems so obvious-

01:02:21.204 --> 01:02:22.873
- None of us are linguists.

01:02:22.873 --> 01:02:25.257
This is all just our thoughts

01:02:25.257 --> 01:02:26.460
from learning a different language

01:02:26.460 --> 01:02:28.606
and from speaking multiple languages.

01:02:28.606 --> 01:02:31.252
But I think the best thought
experiment I can think of is

01:02:31.252 --> 01:02:32.868
like anyone who speaks English,

01:02:32.868 --> 01:02:36.472
like how would you explain
the concept of the word fuck

01:02:36.472 --> 01:02:38.116
to someone who doesn't speak English

01:02:38.116 --> 01:02:39.435
and somebody who didn't grow up here?

01:02:39.435 --> 01:02:40.268
- [Connor] Yeah.

01:02:40.268 --> 01:02:41.101
- That's like, it's,

01:02:41.101 --> 01:02:44.583
I don't even know where I
would begin to start, you know?

01:02:44.583 --> 01:02:47.916
Like, if you don't know, like, you know,

01:02:48.992 --> 01:02:50.397
if you didn't grow up in the culture,

01:02:50.397 --> 01:02:51.991
if you didn't grow up with
people saying it around you,

01:02:51.991 --> 01:02:54.416
hearing that word
everywhere, I'm just like,

01:02:54.416 --> 01:02:58.128
how do I explain the right
way to use the word fuck?

01:02:58.128 --> 01:02:59.618
- I mean, I literally made a video

01:02:59.618 --> 01:03:02.390
'cause they made an entire textbook purely

01:03:02.390 --> 01:03:04.266
for the word fuck.

01:03:04.266 --> 01:03:05.099
- Yeah, I've seen this.

01:03:05.099 --> 01:03:06.981
- It's like a 70 page textbook

01:03:06.981 --> 01:03:09.071
that goes through all the
different ways you can use fuck.

01:03:09.071 --> 01:03:11.267
And like, I thought it was a
gag at first when I bought it.

01:03:11.267 --> 01:03:13.393
But then when I actually
started reading, I was like,

01:03:13.393 --> 01:03:14.812
okay, that's how you explain it.

01:03:14.812 --> 01:03:16.689
Apparently there is a way to explain it.

01:03:16.689 --> 01:03:18.469
It just takes 70 pages.

01:03:18.469 --> 01:03:20.064
- And the fact that it takes 70 pages

01:03:20.064 --> 01:03:22.731
just shows how complicated it is

01:03:23.793 --> 01:03:25.728
even though for us it's just second nature

01:03:25.728 --> 01:03:27.128
and it just makes sense, right?

01:03:27.128 --> 01:03:28.587
- And like the opposite can be said

01:03:28.587 --> 01:03:30.124
for like Japanese to English, right?

01:03:30.124 --> 01:03:31.818
Like, how do you explain
to an English speaker

01:03:31.818 --> 01:03:33.795
what (speaks Japanese) means?

01:03:33.795 --> 01:03:36.892
Because like it's a purely cultural thing.

01:03:36.892 --> 01:03:38.931
They're like, it makes
complete sense in Japanese.

01:03:38.931 --> 01:03:41.869
But then every time,
like every time in anime

01:03:41.869 --> 01:03:43.351
they say like (speaks Japanese)

01:03:43.351 --> 01:03:46.244
There's always a different
way that someone's translated.

01:03:46.244 --> 01:03:47.184
- It's a different way to translate

01:03:47.184 --> 01:03:50.039
depending on the context of the scene

01:03:50.039 --> 01:03:51.852
or the context of what he's saying it in.

01:03:51.852 --> 01:03:53.848
- Like, saying, I guess so.

01:03:53.848 --> 01:03:55.049
Like, oh, I guess so.

01:03:55.049 --> 01:03:56.757
It's like it's not a thing in Japanese.

01:03:56.757 --> 01:03:57.590
Can't translate it.

01:03:57.590 --> 01:04:00.263
It's not even even in Welsh.

01:04:00.263 --> 01:04:02.020
It's such an English thing that,

01:04:02.020 --> 01:04:05.906
'cause none of the words mean
what they mean altogether.

01:04:05.906 --> 01:04:08.240
It's a weird concept that we just make up.

01:04:08.240 --> 01:04:09.106
We do that with a lot.

01:04:09.106 --> 01:04:10.290
- I find that shit fascinating, dude.

01:04:10.290 --> 01:04:11.123
- Bussin'.

01:04:11.123 --> 01:04:12.053
- Yeah, bussin'.

01:04:12.053 --> 01:04:12.886
- Bussin'.

01:04:12.886 --> 01:04:13.969
(everyone laughs)

01:04:13.969 --> 01:04:15.552
- The fuck is that?

01:04:17.052 --> 01:04:18.834
- I literally just
learned that word today.

01:04:18.834 --> 01:04:20.552
Man, I couldn't even keep
up with my own language.

01:04:20.552 --> 01:04:22.049
How the fuck are Japanese people meant

01:04:22.049 --> 01:04:24.382
to keep up with my language?

01:04:25.326 --> 01:04:27.020
- But going back to anime.

01:04:27.020 --> 01:04:28.291
- Yeah, going back to anime.

01:04:28.291 --> 01:04:30.488
- I appreciate voice acting so much more.

01:04:30.488 --> 01:04:32.042
I don't know if you,

01:04:32.042 --> 01:04:34.388
I watched like two episodes of "Yasuke."

01:04:34.388 --> 01:04:35.914
That was pretty good.

01:04:35.914 --> 01:04:36.990
The voice acting I really enjoyed.

01:04:36.990 --> 01:04:39.160
- I need to watch that as well.

01:04:39.160 --> 01:04:42.259
- From two episodes, I wasn't
really sold on the story.

01:04:42.259 --> 01:04:45.283
Again, I knew about the, if
you don't know about "Yasuke,"

01:04:45.283 --> 01:04:47.900
the plot is essentially Nobunaga

01:04:47.900 --> 01:04:50.706
way back in the Oda period had-

01:04:50.706 --> 01:04:51.544
- Sengoku period.

01:04:51.544 --> 01:04:52.497
- Sengoku period, sorry.

01:04:52.497 --> 01:04:56.799
Sengoku period had just
met a black guy at a market

01:04:56.799 --> 01:04:58.603
and was like, "I want
him to fight for me."

01:04:58.603 --> 01:05:00.288
- Based on a real person as well.

01:05:00.288 --> 01:05:04.222
- Was one of his closest
like allies, I guess.

01:05:04.222 --> 01:05:06.973
And the story kind of expands on it.

01:05:06.973 --> 01:05:09.227
But I saw a bunch of this on YouTube.

01:05:09.227 --> 01:05:11.457
I thought this would be
a fucking badass anime.

01:05:11.457 --> 01:05:15.039
Shit you not like two
weeks later got announced.

01:05:15.039 --> 01:05:15.872
And I was like,

01:05:15.872 --> 01:05:19.409
"Wow, I guess I should
start wishing for things."

01:05:19.409 --> 01:05:21.379
I highly encourage you
to go read up about it.

01:05:21.379 --> 01:05:23.797
It's super interesting and
you wouldn't expect it.

01:05:23.797 --> 01:05:26.265
- It's also done by LeSean Thomas.

01:05:26.265 --> 01:05:28.082
- Yeah, done by LeSean Thomas.

01:05:28.082 --> 01:05:29.628
- I don't know who the
animation studio is.

01:05:29.628 --> 01:05:30.461
- MAPPA.

01:05:30.461 --> 01:05:31.294
- Oh, is it MAPPA?

01:05:31.294 --> 01:05:34.076
- But I do think that
if you want to learn,

01:05:34.076 --> 01:05:36.309
this is not like the best of explaining,

01:05:36.309 --> 01:05:38.145
at least from the first
two episodes, I was like,

01:05:38.145 --> 01:05:40.846
"This is wildly different from-"

01:05:40.846 --> 01:05:42.425
- You said there was like magic.

01:05:42.425 --> 01:05:44.238
- There's magic, there's mechs and stuff.

01:05:44.238 --> 01:05:45.321
And it's like-

01:05:45.321 --> 01:05:48.269
- I'm pretty sure that
didn't exist in feudal Japan.

01:05:48.269 --> 01:05:49.102
- Well yeah, I mean-

01:05:49.102 --> 01:05:51.188
- That was literally LeSean
Thomas going, "fuck it."

01:05:51.188 --> 01:05:52.276
- I get it, you're an anime-

01:05:52.276 --> 01:05:53.158
- Throw everything in.

01:05:53.158 --> 01:05:53.991
- Go crazy with it.

01:05:53.991 --> 01:05:55.958
But in some aspects I'm also like,

01:05:55.958 --> 01:05:59.917
this is such a fucking
badass story by itself

01:05:59.917 --> 01:06:02.092
that it doesn't need anything added.

01:06:02.092 --> 01:06:04.295
It's so Goddamn, like
the best parts of like,

01:06:04.295 --> 01:06:05.970
again I've only watched two out of six,

01:06:05.970 --> 01:06:07.648
the best parts of the first two episodes

01:06:07.648 --> 01:06:09.885
where the parts were like pre,

01:06:09.885 --> 01:06:11.294
'cause there's a time skip,

01:06:11.294 --> 01:06:13.825
pre-time skip where there's
like no magic or shit

01:06:13.825 --> 01:06:15.856
where he's just fighting sword to sword.

01:06:15.856 --> 01:06:18.328
Man to man combat, it's so Goddamn good.

01:06:18.328 --> 01:06:19.809
And the story and it builds on all the,

01:06:19.809 --> 01:06:22.767
obviously back then there'd
be a lot of issues with race.

01:06:22.767 --> 01:06:24.453
- Yeah, of course.

01:06:24.453 --> 01:06:25.661
Of course.

01:06:25.661 --> 01:06:28.093
- They weren't too happy about
it when Nobunaga was like,

01:06:28.093 --> 01:06:30.409
"This is my best friend."

01:06:30.409 --> 01:06:32.908
You know, and building on
that was so interesting.

01:06:32.908 --> 01:06:34.785
And I thought like the best
parts of the anime were that.

01:06:34.785 --> 01:06:37.241
And again, yeah, the
story is just so cool.

01:06:37.241 --> 01:06:38.092
Like, go read up about it.

01:06:38.092 --> 01:06:39.858
There's tons of YouTube videos about it.

01:06:39.858 --> 01:06:42.289
- I actually like went and
like fucking researched.

01:06:42.289 --> 01:06:43.322
- It's so fucking cool.

01:06:43.322 --> 01:06:44.299
- The real life Yasuke just

01:06:44.299 --> 01:06:45.619
'cause like I had no fucking idea.

01:06:45.619 --> 01:06:46.536
- It's a badass story.

01:06:46.536 --> 01:06:48.537
- Oh yeah, it's fucking badass.

01:06:48.537 --> 01:06:51.445
It's like it's so bizarre
that it could be fictional.

01:06:51.445 --> 01:06:55.320
- Do you feel like the mech
and magic aspects added

01:06:55.320 --> 01:06:57.433
to that story or do you
think it felt out of place?

01:06:57.433 --> 01:06:59.985
- For me personally I
didn't really enjoy it.

01:06:59.985 --> 01:07:00.818
I was hoping-

01:07:00.818 --> 01:07:01.745
- You just wanted-

01:07:01.745 --> 01:07:04.067
- The story of Yasuke,
that's what I wanted.

01:07:04.067 --> 01:07:05.954
- You wanted like a "Samurai
Champloo" style like story.

01:07:05.954 --> 01:07:07.993
- Kind of, I mean, but then again, like-

01:07:07.993 --> 01:07:09.485
- Is that historically accurate?

01:07:09.485 --> 01:07:10.318
- No, no.

01:07:10.318 --> 01:07:11.651
(everyone laughs)

01:07:11.651 --> 01:07:12.901
- Breakdancing samurai.

01:07:12.901 --> 01:07:14.958
- There weren't magic and mechs.

01:07:14.958 --> 01:07:16.437
- The music in the first two episodes

01:07:16.437 --> 01:07:17.652
is pretty fucking good.

01:07:17.652 --> 01:07:18.517
- Yeah, exactly.

01:07:18.517 --> 01:07:19.350
- It's really good.

01:07:19.350 --> 01:07:21.163
The voice acting, top fucking notch.

01:07:21.163 --> 01:07:22.726
Even the Japanese is really good.

01:07:22.726 --> 01:07:24.264
And like, you know, even in the Japanese,

01:07:24.264 --> 01:07:26.597
Yasuke is played by a black Japanese guy,

01:07:26.597 --> 01:07:27.664
which is insane to see.

01:07:27.664 --> 01:07:28.497
- [Garnt] That's awesome.

01:07:28.497 --> 01:07:30.137
- It's normally not on the priority list.

01:07:30.137 --> 01:07:31.720
- Yeah.

01:07:31.720 --> 01:07:33.314
- You know, it's really
cool seeing that, you know.

01:07:33.314 --> 01:07:34.898
Why wouldn't you want that?

01:07:34.898 --> 01:07:37.442
Yeah, I mean, everything
else about it, I was digging.

01:07:37.442 --> 01:07:38.275
Everything.

01:07:38.275 --> 01:07:40.242
You know, I haven't really been motivated

01:07:40.242 --> 01:07:41.712
to watch the rest of it.

01:07:41.712 --> 01:07:43.843
But I think that's 'cause the
mechs thing's kinda put me off

01:07:43.843 --> 01:07:44.895
and the magic and stuff.

01:07:44.895 --> 01:07:45.886
Oh man.

01:07:45.886 --> 01:07:48.574
- I mean, the short clips
I watched of it was,

01:07:48.574 --> 01:07:50.917
like I didn't realize it was like gonna be

01:07:50.917 --> 01:07:52.813
that fucking bloody and gory as well.

01:07:52.813 --> 01:07:53.646
- Oh, dude, it's good.

01:07:53.646 --> 01:07:55.038
- Like, some of the
scenes like reminded me

01:07:55.038 --> 01:07:57.450
of like a 90s OVA, like
"Ninja Scroll" level.

01:07:57.450 --> 01:07:58.584
- Feels like "Kill Bill" at some points.

01:07:58.584 --> 01:08:00.364
- Yeah, it was like "Kill
Bill," "Ninja Scroll"

01:08:00.364 --> 01:08:01.634
like levels of like, ooh!

01:08:01.634 --> 01:08:03.714
Ooh, that's brutal!

01:08:03.714 --> 01:08:04.547
- It's so good.

01:08:04.547 --> 01:08:05.380
- I love it.

01:08:05.380 --> 01:08:07.184
- Yeah, I still haven't seen it, but I-

01:08:07.184 --> 01:08:08.359
- Check it out.

01:08:08.359 --> 01:08:10.223
- I will, I will definitely check it out.

01:08:10.223 --> 01:08:11.721
- You'll know if it's for you
in the first two episodes.

01:08:11.721 --> 01:08:14.687
- Because like I really like
LeSean Thomas' work anyway,

01:08:14.687 --> 01:08:15.520
so I was gonna watch it.

01:08:15.520 --> 01:08:18.042
It's just hard to find time
with all the fucking anime

01:08:18.042 --> 01:08:19.704
in the season and everything

01:08:19.704 --> 01:08:21.182
which you two don't know about.

01:08:21.182 --> 01:08:22.015
- Can't relate.

01:08:22.015 --> 01:08:23.006
- I've been meaning to watch a bunch.

01:08:23.006 --> 01:08:24.336
I've been meaning to watch "86."

01:08:24.336 --> 01:08:27.468
- "86" is actually really good.

01:08:27.468 --> 01:08:30.808
I probably say that's my favorite.

01:08:30.808 --> 01:08:31.844
Oh, I can't say favorite.

01:08:31.844 --> 01:08:32.677
It's hard.

01:08:32.677 --> 01:08:34.888
It's definitely top three
of my favorite anime

01:08:34.888 --> 01:08:36.113
out this season right now.

01:08:36.113 --> 01:08:40.654
And it just feels good to
have an original mecha show

01:08:40.654 --> 01:08:42.687
that just gives me the same feeling

01:08:42.687 --> 01:08:44.421
as like some of the OG mecha shows

01:08:44.421 --> 01:08:46.438
that made me really,
really like the genre.

01:08:46.438 --> 01:08:47.822
Because it feels like it's been so long

01:08:47.822 --> 01:08:51.578
since we've just had a
non-Gundam, non-Code Geass,

01:08:51.578 --> 01:08:53.783
or non-big franchise mecha show

01:08:53.783 --> 01:08:56.087
that has actually been
really, really good.

01:08:56.087 --> 01:08:57.928
Because most of the mecha shows I remember

01:08:57.928 --> 01:08:59.627
that's been coming out
recently have either been

01:08:59.627 --> 01:09:01.335
like "Darling in the
Franxx" where I get invested

01:09:01.335 --> 01:09:04.362
and it kind of does shit that falls flat,

01:09:04.362 --> 01:09:05.792
or like I've really enjoyed-

01:09:05.792 --> 01:09:07.439
- And then triggers like let me introduce.

01:09:07.439 --> 01:09:08.548
(everyone laughs)

01:09:08.548 --> 01:09:10.927
- And then you've had
things like "SSSS Gridman"

01:09:10.927 --> 01:09:12.594
which fucking amazing show,

01:09:12.594 --> 01:09:14.252
but it's like, it's a mecha show,

01:09:14.252 --> 01:09:16.021
but it's also a bit tokusatsu.

01:09:16.021 --> 01:09:18.090
So, it's not like, it's like-

01:09:18.090 --> 01:09:19.827
- It's not like a vanilla
mecha show, right?

01:09:19.827 --> 01:09:21.035
- Yeah, yeah.

01:09:21.035 --> 01:09:21.868
- Vanilla.

01:09:21.868 --> 01:09:23.981
- Vanilla mecha where it's
just mecha and that's it.

01:09:23.981 --> 01:09:26.195
- But "86," you know,
gives me the same feelings

01:09:26.195 --> 01:09:29.517
of when I first watched "Code Geass"

01:09:29.517 --> 01:09:31.719
or the mechs that I
watched in the mid-2000s

01:09:31.719 --> 01:09:34.847
that really made me
love the fucking genre.

01:09:34.847 --> 01:09:35.948
It's still early days.

01:09:35.948 --> 01:09:37.837
I don't know if it's
gonna be like 24 episodes

01:09:37.837 --> 01:09:40.626
or 12 episodes where there's
gonna be a complete story.

01:09:40.626 --> 01:09:41.508
I'm really hoping so.

01:09:41.508 --> 01:09:44.595
But it's just really, really good.

01:09:44.595 --> 01:09:45.428
- Fair enough.

01:09:45.428 --> 01:09:46.832
- I mean, do you know
the story of it at all?

01:09:46.832 --> 01:09:47.665
- I don't want to know anything.

01:09:47.665 --> 01:09:48.632
All I've heard that it's good.

01:09:48.632 --> 01:09:51.173
And I'm gonna watch it.

01:09:51.173 --> 01:09:53.493
- Just go into it blind
is the best way I think.

01:09:53.493 --> 01:09:56.122
- I watched "The Way of the
Husband" on Netflix as well.

01:09:56.122 --> 01:09:56.955
- "The Way of the Househusband."

01:09:56.955 --> 01:09:58.163
- That's it, yeah.

01:09:58.163 --> 01:09:59.997
I mean, I enjoyed it a lot.

01:09:59.997 --> 01:10:01.469
I thought it was very funny.

01:10:01.469 --> 01:10:02.302
I haven't had an anime

01:10:02.302 --> 01:10:03.933
that made me laugh out loud constantly.

01:10:03.933 --> 01:10:05.056
- Yeah, it's hilarious.

01:10:05.056 --> 01:10:05.889
- For like two hours.

01:10:05.889 --> 01:10:07.979
I mean, I thought it was gonna be

01:10:07.979 --> 01:10:09.950
like 10 episodes, 24 minutes,

01:10:09.950 --> 01:10:12.163
but it's like five episodes
of like 12, 15 minutes.

01:10:12.163 --> 01:10:14.298
- Yeah, I only saw three episodes.

01:10:14.298 --> 01:10:15.649
I was like, I got the rest
of the season to binge.

01:10:15.649 --> 01:10:16.755
I didn't know it was only five episodes.

01:10:16.755 --> 01:10:18.088
- It's five episodes.

01:10:18.088 --> 01:10:21.444
It kinda sucked that it literally
just like, it just ended.

01:10:21.444 --> 01:10:23.104
It was like, there's the last skit.

01:10:23.104 --> 01:10:23.937
It's done.

01:10:23.937 --> 01:10:24.770
Bye bye.

01:10:24.770 --> 01:10:25.989
And then it was like, there
was no ending or anything.

01:10:25.989 --> 01:10:28.217
It wasn't like, "See ya
next time" or anything.

01:10:28.217 --> 01:10:29.696
It was just like, "Okay, skit over.

01:10:29.696 --> 01:10:31.389
"Go the fuck home, get outta here."

01:10:31.389 --> 01:10:33.478
- 'Cause each of the chapters
in the manga are really,

01:10:33.478 --> 01:10:36.783
really short, like maybe like
five, six pages like max.

01:10:36.783 --> 01:10:39.317
- I thought the pacing was fantastic.

01:10:39.317 --> 01:10:40.891
I knew obviously it caused
a lot of controversy

01:10:40.891 --> 01:10:41.724
with the animation.

01:10:41.724 --> 01:10:44.839
I saw a lot of people
complaining on Twitter.

01:10:44.839 --> 01:10:46.282
I couldn't decide.

01:10:46.282 --> 01:10:47.154
I flip-flopped.

01:10:47.154 --> 01:10:49.329
There was some sketches where
I felt they did really good.

01:10:49.329 --> 01:10:50.764
And there was some where I'm like,

01:10:50.764 --> 01:10:53.141
"Holy fuck, this was so lazily done."

01:10:53.141 --> 01:10:54.457
And it depended on the sketch.

01:10:54.457 --> 01:10:57.470
- Well, I think it just went
down to the classification

01:10:57.470 --> 01:10:59.118
'cause I think we've
briefly talked about this

01:10:59.118 --> 01:11:01.792
on "Trash Taste After Dark"
where like my opinion of it was

01:11:01.792 --> 01:11:06.134
that it's not so much an
anime in the traditional sense

01:11:06.134 --> 01:11:08.321
where it's basically just a motion comic.

01:11:08.321 --> 01:11:09.668
It is just a motion-

01:11:09.668 --> 01:11:11.374
- I wish it was labeled
that and advertised as that

01:11:11.374 --> 01:11:13.717
instead of anime adaptation.

01:11:13.717 --> 01:11:15.066
- But I feel if you've labeled it

01:11:15.066 --> 01:11:16.863
as "motion comic adaptation,"

01:11:16.863 --> 01:11:18.854
then I think less people would
have been interested in it,

01:11:18.854 --> 01:11:19.937
unfortunately.

01:11:19.937 --> 01:11:22.648
- True, but then also
you set this expectation

01:11:22.648 --> 01:11:24.704
that this is gonna be a
thing that might happen.

01:11:24.704 --> 01:11:25.729
- Because I feel like it was that

01:11:25.729 --> 01:11:27.409
and it being on Netflix as well.

01:11:27.409 --> 01:11:28.566
Netflix really picking this up,

01:11:28.566 --> 01:11:31.615
which gave it like people
preconceived expectations.

01:11:31.615 --> 01:11:35.021
'Cause to me, I watched it, I
thought it was funny as fuck.

01:11:35.021 --> 01:11:37.216
I thought the animation
worked for some of the jokes.

01:11:37.216 --> 01:11:39.538
- Again, like, it's up there with, like,

01:11:39.538 --> 01:11:41.791
I thought it was just as funny
as like "Sakamoto" for me,

01:11:41.791 --> 01:11:43.249
if not funnier.

01:11:43.249 --> 01:11:44.617
Like, it was so Goddamn funny,

01:11:44.617 --> 01:11:45.713
and it scratched that itch

01:11:45.713 --> 01:11:46.968
that I didn't know I was longing for.

01:11:46.968 --> 01:11:47.801
- Yeah.

01:11:47.801 --> 01:11:49.400
- Every single episode
I was fucking cackling,

01:11:49.400 --> 01:11:50.635
laughing out loud alone.

01:11:50.635 --> 01:11:53.041
- It's like that weird
like surrealist comedy.

01:11:53.041 --> 01:11:53.874
- It's so good.

01:11:53.874 --> 01:11:55.392
- You just don't know
what he's gonna say next,

01:11:55.392 --> 01:11:56.350
what's gonna happen.

01:11:56.350 --> 01:11:58.479
- Every time you feel like you
figured out how absurd he is,

01:11:58.479 --> 01:11:59.585
he just does something else.

01:11:59.585 --> 01:12:01.029
And you're like, this is fucking funny.

01:12:01.029 --> 01:12:03.215
If you haven't watched
it, please go watch it.

01:12:03.215 --> 01:12:05.610
It's just about like a Yakuza
member who gets married

01:12:05.610 --> 01:12:06.443
and straightens out

01:12:06.443 --> 01:12:08.983
and has become a housewife, househusband.

01:12:08.983 --> 01:12:10.425
And yeah, it's just really funny.

01:12:10.425 --> 01:12:12.244
But it would have been at like,

01:12:12.244 --> 01:12:14.113
it would have been a
nine or a 10 for me if,

01:12:14.113 --> 01:12:15.604
again, like, I don't know.

01:12:15.604 --> 01:12:19.338
I don't really like the add
of the motion comic style.

01:12:19.338 --> 01:12:20.972
- Do you think it would have been funnier

01:12:20.972 --> 01:12:23.139
with say just mediocre adaptation?

01:12:23.139 --> 01:12:23.972
- Honestly, yeah.

01:12:23.972 --> 01:12:25.555
- Mediocre animation.

01:12:25.555 --> 01:12:26.481
- Genuinely, yeah.

01:12:26.481 --> 01:12:28.726
'Cause there was so
little animation on anyway

01:12:28.726 --> 01:12:30.020
and there's just times I'm like,

01:12:30.020 --> 01:12:31.968
I wish they just did a little bit on this

01:12:31.968 --> 01:12:33.689
just to help sell the joke.

01:12:33.689 --> 01:12:36.688
- I feel like the lack of
animation helps sell some jokes

01:12:36.688 --> 01:12:37.521
if anything.

01:12:37.521 --> 01:12:38.354
- I agree, I agree.

01:12:38.354 --> 01:12:39.187
- Just some of them.

01:12:39.187 --> 01:12:41.180
Just because some of it
just looks ridiculous.

01:12:41.180 --> 01:12:43.575
And that to me just made it more funny.

01:12:43.575 --> 01:12:46.750
- But imagine this anime
in like "Nichijou" style.

01:12:46.750 --> 01:12:49.373
- Yeah, but like name another comedy anime

01:12:49.373 --> 01:12:51.303
that's on "Nichijou" level.

01:12:51.303 --> 01:12:53.163
- There isn't, but I'm just saying like,

01:12:53.163 --> 01:12:54.061
if you had the choice.

01:12:54.061 --> 01:12:56.778
- No, if I had the choice between that,

01:12:56.778 --> 01:12:58.551
I'd always go for fucking
"Nichijou" animation

01:12:58.551 --> 01:13:00.041
even like "KonoSuba" animation.

01:13:00.041 --> 01:13:03.265
'Cause "KonoSuba," I think a
lot of people underestimate

01:13:03.265 --> 01:13:05.453
how good the character
animation in "KonoSuba" is.

01:13:05.453 --> 01:13:08.306
That really sold so much of
the voice acting performance

01:13:08.306 --> 01:13:11.844
where a lot of other comedy
anime I feel have fallen flat

01:13:11.844 --> 01:13:14.045
because you have amazing
voice acting performance,

01:13:14.045 --> 01:13:15.268
you have amazing source material,

01:13:15.268 --> 01:13:17.624
and the animation is just like-

01:13:17.624 --> 01:13:18.457
- Okay.

01:13:18.457 --> 01:13:19.904
- The most okay animation.

01:13:19.904 --> 01:13:23.379
It really does nothing to
enhance the source material.

01:13:23.379 --> 01:13:25.316
- Maybe I'm being too
hard on it. I don't know.

01:13:25.316 --> 01:13:27.438
I think I was just shocked
at how little there was.

01:13:27.438 --> 01:13:28.271
- Yeah.

01:13:28.271 --> 01:13:29.260
Whereas with "Way of the Househusband,"

01:13:29.260 --> 01:13:30.683
it had amazing voice acting obviously,

01:13:30.683 --> 01:13:31.765
had amazing source material,

01:13:31.765 --> 01:13:33.995
and I feel like because they didn't try,

01:13:33.995 --> 01:13:37.069
it kind of like suited that
comedy style perfectly.

01:13:37.069 --> 01:13:39.703
And I feel like to me,

01:13:39.703 --> 01:13:42.255
if you couldn't have amazing animation,

01:13:42.255 --> 01:13:44.637
I would have preferred to
have it have like just,

01:13:44.637 --> 01:13:46.383
not even like bad animation,

01:13:46.383 --> 01:13:49.516
just like a very unique
style of limited animation

01:13:49.516 --> 01:13:52.162
that really helps sell some of the weirder

01:13:52.162 --> 01:13:53.909
and more ridiculous parts of the manga

01:13:53.909 --> 01:13:54.968
'cause it is a ridiculous manga,

01:13:54.968 --> 01:13:57.415
and I feel like the animation
style helped accentuate

01:13:57.415 --> 01:13:59.631
some of the ridiculous moments to me.

01:13:59.631 --> 01:14:00.895
- Yeah, there's some
moments where I was like,

01:14:00.895 --> 01:14:02.985
"Yeah, okay, this joke
works with this animation."

01:14:02.985 --> 01:14:03.818
There's others where I'm like,

01:14:03.818 --> 01:14:06.900
"This really needed more to
help sell some of this joke."

01:14:06.900 --> 01:14:07.733
I don't know, personally.

01:14:07.733 --> 01:14:08.985
- I feel like maybe a mix could have

01:14:08.985 --> 01:14:11.662
like really, really propelled it.

01:14:11.662 --> 01:14:13.370
- Have you seen clips of the,

01:14:13.370 --> 01:14:15.518
there's a Japanese live action adaptation.

01:14:15.518 --> 01:14:16.799
Have you seen this?
- [Garnt] I have not.

01:14:16.799 --> 01:14:17.785
- I've seen it, yeah.

01:14:17.785 --> 01:14:19.741
- It's so bad!

01:14:19.741 --> 01:14:20.949
It's so funny!

01:14:20.949 --> 01:14:22.976
It's like (laughs)

01:14:22.976 --> 01:14:23.809
- It's tragic.

01:14:23.809 --> 01:14:24.642
- Wait, what's that?

01:14:24.642 --> 01:14:25.475
Describe it to me.

01:14:25.475 --> 01:14:26.780
- It's just like, okay, the main guy,

01:14:26.780 --> 01:14:28.258
it looks like a cosplay.

01:14:28.258 --> 01:14:29.091
It doesn't look-

01:14:29.091 --> 01:14:29.924
- It is a cosplay!

01:14:29.924 --> 01:14:34.386
- Like, it looks like a cosplay,
not like an actual actor.

01:14:34.386 --> 01:14:38.161
Like, the guy isn't like built enough.

01:14:38.161 --> 01:14:40.540
- It is like "Full Metal
Alchemist" live action level.

01:14:40.540 --> 01:14:41.999
- Oh my God!

01:14:41.999 --> 01:14:43.722
- And then his friend in the anime

01:14:43.722 --> 01:14:44.834
who was really young and supposed to be

01:14:44.834 --> 01:14:47.524
like the young gang member
looks really fucking old

01:14:47.524 --> 01:14:48.766
and like-

01:14:48.766 --> 01:14:50.528
- I didn't watch it like fully.

01:14:50.528 --> 01:14:52.664
I only watched like
clips of it on YouTube,

01:14:52.664 --> 01:14:54.432
and I was just like, "Oh no."

01:14:54.432 --> 01:14:55.349
- It's bad.

01:14:57.015 --> 01:14:59.624
I watched the same skit,
both of them and compared.

01:14:59.624 --> 01:15:03.360
The humor wasn't nearly as
good in the live action.

01:15:03.360 --> 01:15:05.398
Like, I don't know why.

01:15:05.398 --> 01:15:06.466
I feel like they didn't like,

01:15:06.466 --> 01:15:07.881
'cause with animation you
can really sell the absurdity

01:15:07.881 --> 01:15:09.115
and the live action one-

01:15:09.115 --> 01:15:09.948
- That's the point, right?

01:15:09.948 --> 01:15:11.910
- Yeah, but it didn't work very well.

01:15:11.910 --> 01:15:13.130
- Yeah, I feel like-

01:15:13.130 --> 01:15:15.567
- Also Japanese acting in TV shows,

01:15:15.567 --> 01:15:17.465
I don't know how they are so bad,

01:15:17.465 --> 01:15:19.633
but I've never seen
Japanese acting in a TV show

01:15:19.633 --> 01:15:21.313
and been like, "That's fantastic."

01:15:21.313 --> 01:15:22.955
- Unless it's like Ken Watanabe.

01:15:22.955 --> 01:15:24.663
- Literally, it's like he's the only one.

01:15:24.663 --> 01:15:26.089
I feel bad saying that

01:15:26.089 --> 01:15:27.747
'cause I feel like that's
such a broad statement,

01:15:27.747 --> 01:15:30.185
but I've watched so much Japanese TV

01:15:30.185 --> 01:15:32.896
and all the drama acting is appalling.

01:15:32.896 --> 01:15:33.729
- Yeah, it's not good.

01:15:33.729 --> 01:15:34.687
- It's so bad.

01:15:34.687 --> 01:15:36.148
- Especially in like the live action.

01:15:36.148 --> 01:15:38.713
Like, especially when a
live action anime adaptation

01:15:38.713 --> 01:15:41.784
of a Japanese TV show or a Japanese anime,

01:15:41.784 --> 01:15:46.784
it's always, it's so weird
seeing live action actors try

01:15:46.800 --> 01:15:48.391
to act like anime characters

01:15:48.391 --> 01:15:49.915
or doing like the anime style acting.

01:15:49.915 --> 01:15:51.989
- 'Cause you watch like Korean dramas

01:15:51.989 --> 01:15:54.602
and Korean adaptations and
stuff, and it's so much better.

01:15:54.602 --> 01:15:56.935
I watched like "Sweet Home,"

01:15:58.143 --> 01:16:01.075
the web tune adaptation into Netflix,

01:16:01.075 --> 01:16:02.843
and the actors were fucking amazing in it.

01:16:02.843 --> 01:16:03.849
- There's a live action adaptation?

01:16:03.849 --> 01:16:05.515
- Live action.
- Oh shit, I gotta watch that.

01:16:05.515 --> 01:16:06.598
- And the acting was really fucking good.

01:16:06.598 --> 01:16:09.286
Like, every single time
I've watched a Korean movie

01:16:09.286 --> 01:16:10.710
or Korean drama, I'm always so impressed

01:16:10.710 --> 01:16:13.285
at how fucking good, not to
say that the actors are bad.

01:16:13.285 --> 01:16:15.251
But I just thought for
some reason, I'm like,

01:16:15.251 --> 01:16:16.247
oh, I've seen Japanese acting.

01:16:16.247 --> 01:16:20.330
It's gonna be over the
top dramatic all the time.

01:16:21.894 --> 01:16:24.105
- I feel like, especially in recent years,

01:16:24.105 --> 01:16:28.018
Korean movies and Korean dramas
and shows have just like,

01:16:28.018 --> 01:16:29.185
they are like,

01:16:30.168 --> 01:16:33.581
they are way ahead of like
Japanese J dramas and J movies.

01:16:33.581 --> 01:16:36.227
- So many movies where I'm like
fucking compared to English,

01:16:36.227 --> 01:16:37.393
it like shits on them.

01:16:37.393 --> 01:16:38.226
Like, some of the,

01:16:38.226 --> 01:16:39.871
like "Old Boy," like I love that movie.

01:16:39.871 --> 01:16:40.704
- Fucking.

01:16:40.704 --> 01:16:43.458
And that's actually based
on a manga, did you know?

01:16:43.458 --> 01:16:44.291
- I didn't know that.

01:16:44.291 --> 01:16:45.124
- Oh really?

01:16:45.124 --> 01:16:47.116
- Yeah, "Old Boy" was originally a manga.

01:16:47.116 --> 01:16:48.975
It got adapted into a Korean movie.

01:16:48.975 --> 01:16:50.189
- Oh, that's cool.

01:16:50.189 --> 01:16:52.285
- That movie is like one
of my favorite movies

01:16:52.285 --> 01:16:53.118
of all time.

01:16:53.118 --> 01:16:53.951
- It's fucking amazing.

01:16:53.951 --> 01:16:55.762
- The acting is so Goddamn
good in that movie.

01:16:55.762 --> 01:16:57.268
- The cinematography is fantastic.

01:16:57.268 --> 01:16:59.340
- That's one of the greatest
foreign films of all time,

01:16:59.340 --> 01:17:02.625
and it's, you know, it's up
there with like "Parasite"

01:17:02.625 --> 01:17:07.091
as like, to me, as one of the
best Korean movies I've seen.

01:17:07.091 --> 01:17:09.669
There are so many good
Korean movies, right?

01:17:09.669 --> 01:17:13.262
And I feel like people
are now just figuring out

01:17:13.262 --> 01:17:15.135
that man, Koreans make good movies.

01:17:15.135 --> 01:17:16.057
- Oh yeah, they're very good.

